<div class="hero">
<h1>🕵️ Too Clueless To Care?</h1>
<div>Practice: how do you respond when someone says "I can't do it"?</div>
<div class="q">When someone says "I'm clueless," how can we know if it is true?</div>
</div>

<h2>🔎 Three Questions to Ask Yourself</h2>
<div class="checks">
<div class="check"><b>1 · Effort</b>Has this person actually tried, or do they hand the task over immediately?</div>
<div class="check"><b>2 · Learning</b>After being shown, do they improve, or does the "problem" never change?</div>
<div class="check"><b>3 · The ask</b>Do they ask for help, or do they ask you to take over?</div>
</div>

<h2>🎭 Scenarios: What Would You Say?</h2>
<p>Read the situation. Say your answer out loud first, then open the sample answers.</p>

<div class="scn">
<div class="scn-head">① EHS · The incident report</div>
<div class="scn-body">
<p class="sit">A production supervisor has had three minor incidents on his shift this quarter. Each time he tells the safety specialist the same thing, and each time the specialist ends up writing the whole report.</p>
<p class="heard">"I'm just not good at writing reports. You do it so much better."</p>
<p class="ask">❓ What would you say?</p>
<details><summary>👀 Show sample answers</summary>
<div class="ans">
<div class="r"><b>Communicate</b>"I've noticed that I've written the last three reports. I'd like to share that task."</div>
<div class="r b2"><b>Set expectations</b>"I'll send you the template. You write the first draft by tomorrow, and we'll review it together."</div>
<div class="r b3"><b>Don't take over</b>"I can help with the wording, but I can't write it for you. You were there, so you know what happened."</div>
<div class="clue">🔎 Clue: it is a pattern (three times), nothing changes, and the request is "do it for me," not "help me."</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<div class="scn">
<div class="scn-head">② HR · The difficult conversation</div>
<div class="scn-body">
<p class="sit">A department manager sends every performance problem in his team to HR. He never speaks to the employee first, and then he asks HR what to do next.</p>
<p class="heard">"I'm not good with difficult conversations. That's really an HR thing, isn't it?"</p>
<p class="ask">❓ What would you say?</p>
<details><summary>👀 Show sample answers</summary>
<div class="ans">
<div class="r"><b>Communicate</b>"Many managers find these conversations uncomfortable. It's normal, and it's also part of leading a team."</div>
<div class="r b2"><b>Set expectations</b>"You have the first conversation this week. Afterward, we can meet and decide the next step together."</div>
<div class="r b3"><b>Don't take over</b>"I can coach you and sit in if it gets formal, but I won't have the first conversation for you."</div>
<div class="clue">🔎 Clue: discomfort is real, but the person avoids the task completely and uses "not my thing" as a permanent excuse.</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<div class="scn">
<div class="scn-head">③ IT · The same password problem</div>
<div class="scn-body">
<p class="sit">A colleague calls the help desk almost every week with the same problem: she can't connect to the VPN. IT has shown her the steps three times, and she has never written them down.</p>
<p class="heard">"I'm hopeless with computers. Can you just do it remotely, like last time?"</p>
<p class="ask">❓ What would you say?</p>
<details><summary>👀 Show sample answers</summary>
<div class="ans">
<div class="r"><b>Communicate</b>"I know it's frustrating. Since this has happened a few times, I think a short guide will save us both time."</div>
<div class="r b2"><b>Set expectations</b>"I'll walk you through it one more time. This time, write down each step, and next time you try first."</div>
<div class="r b3"><b>Don't take over</b>"I'm not going to do it remotely today, but I'll stay on the line while you do it."</div>
<div class="clue">🔎 Clue: she has been shown three times and still has no notes. She isn't learning, and the pattern keeps repeating.</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<div class="scn">
<div class="scn-head">④ Import / Export · The customs declaration</div>
<div class="scn-body">
<p class="sit">A coordinator says customs paperwork is "too complicated." Whenever a shipment needs a declaration or an HS code, he sends it to a teammate, who finishes it in ten minutes.</p>
<p class="heard">"You're so much faster at this. If I do it, it'll take me two hours and I'll probably get it wrong."</p>
<p class="ask">❓ What would you say?</p>
<details><summary>👀 Show sample answers</summary>
<div class="ans">
<div class="r"><b>Communicate</b>"It does take practice, and it's also becoming a habit that I do all of them. Let's change that."</div>
<div class="r b2"><b>Set expectations</b>"For the next shipment, you prepare the draft and I check it. After three shipments, you do it alone."</div>
<div class="r b3"><b>Don't take over</b>"I'm happy to answer questions, but I'm not going to fill in the form for you. It's your shipment."</div>
<div class="clue">🔎 Clue: "You're faster" is a compliment used as an exit. Being slower at first is normal, but the real problem is never starting.</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<div class="scn" style="border-color:#2d6a4f;box-shadow:6px 6px 0 #2d6a4f">
<div class="scn-head" style="background:#2d6a4f;border-color:#2d6a4f">⑤ Is this weaponized incompetence? · The new colleague</div>
<div class="scn-body">
<p class="sit">A colleague joined your team two weeks ago. She asks you to show her how the shipping system works. The next day, she tries it by herself and asks one specific question about an error message.</p>
<p class="heard">"I've never used this system. Could you show me once? I'll try the next one on my own."</p>
<p class="ask">❓ Is this weaponized incompetence? How would you respond?</p>
<details><summary>👀 Show sample answers</summary>
<div class="ans">
<div class="r"><b>Verdict</b>No. She is honest about what she doesn't know, and she asks for a demonstration, not a replacement.</div>
<div class="r b2"><b>Good response</b>"Of course. Watch this one, then you do the next one while I watch."</div>
<div class="r b3"><b>Why it matters</b>If we treat every "I don't know" as an excuse, we discourage honest people from asking for help.</div>
<div class="clue">🔎 Clue: she tries, she improves, and she takes ownership. Compare her with the four people above.</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</div>

<h2>🧰 Take-Away Phrase Bank</h2>
<table class="bank">
<tbody><tr><th>Communicate</th><td>"I've noticed that…" · "I feel like I'm doing most of the…" · "Can we talk about how we share this?"</td></tr>
<tr><th>Set expectations</th><td>"From now on, you…" · "I'll show you once, then it's yours." · "Please send me the draft by…"</td></tr>
<tr><th>Don't take over</th><td>"I can help, but I can't do it for you." · "I'm not going to do this one." · "Let's see how it goes."</td></tr>
<tr><th>Stay kind but firm</th><td>"I'm happy to support you, but…" · "I know it's hard, and I believe you can do it."</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

